  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Community-Based Peacebuilding Initiative</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The EOI is based on the October 2022 resolutions of the Sudan Bishop&#x2019;s Conference in Khartoum, Sudan. Among the significant resolutions agreed upon is the local church&#x2019;s participation in peacebuilding in Sudan. The resolution is aimed at involving the church structures at the grassroots level to actively work to bring peace towards resolving the prolonged existing political and ethnic conflicts among the people of Sudan that have claimed several lives and destroyed properties and infrastructure. The peace programme primarily targets the youths, usually mobilised to cause violence. The initiative will be implemented through church structures that are in contact with communities daily in selected localities of South Kordofan, West Darfur, Blue Nile and Khartoum states. These will mainly involve the catechists, priests, and religious and selected lay leaders in the centres and parishes</narrative>
  </description>
